"remaining_unknowns": [
  "Whether the stromal target is present in EMC's particular myxoid matrix — this has never been measured. ⚠ The surfaceome screen (ART-SURFACE-EXPRESSION) does return FAP selectivity_q = 0.1555 / myxoid 0.0 — but it is DepMap tumour-cell MONOCULTURE with no CAF compartment, so it cannot see the stroma this route targets and does not answer the question. ⛔ AND THE `myxoid 0.0` FIGURE IS NOT AN EMC READING AT ALL (measured 2026-08-07, surfaceome-instrument-limits.json -> L5): n_myxoid = 1 and that single line is ACH-001519, whose EMC identity this repository RETRACTED on 2026-08-05 (Cellosaurus CVCL_1238 records no EWSR1 fusion; DepMap's filtered fusion caller names no FET gene). So the scan holds no EMC observation of FAP for two independent reasons, and the figure must not be quoted as though it bore on EMC.",
  "Whether a stromal-targeted radioligand delivers enough dose to the tumour cells. ⚠ The repository's own BNCT negative generalises here by its own reasoning: a radioligand is dosed per unit VOLUME and delivered per CELL, and EMC is matrix-dominated. That is an argument, not a measurement, and is recorded as one.",
  "⛔ Whether FAP is present in EMC — and as of 2026-08-07 this is an EXTRACTION REQUEST, not a void. A 642-record Europe PMC corpus on FAP radioligands in sarcoma returns ZERO titles or abstracts naming extraskeletal myxoid chondrosarcoma, NR4A3 or EWSR1 — but a proximity scan of its 483 retrieved FULL TEXTS returns one paper that matters: PMID 38964294 / PMC11797935 [FT] scored 133 soft-tissue sarcomas by FAP immunohistochemistry and lists its enrolled subtypes as including "extraskeletal myxoid chondrosarcoma". EMC tissue HAS been stained for FAP; the EMC-specific FAP SCORES were never reported (its only subtype-level analyses are WDLPS and UPS). ⛔⛔ BUT THE CASE COUNT WAS REPORTED ALL ALONG AND IT IS 1: re-read against the PMC full text on 2026-08-29, Table 1 ('Details of all enrolled cases') gives Extraskeletal myxoid chondrosarcoma = 1 of 133. So the surviving ask is: what were that ONE case's intratumoral and marginal FAP scores? ⚠ ANSWERING IT WOULD NOT CLOSE THIS UNKNOWN — two ordinal scores (0-6) on a single specimen is a case-level observation, not a measurement of FAP in EMC. ⚠ The authors also state that in the intratumoral area no CAF marker could distinguish CAFs from sarcoma cells, so an intratumoral score is not a reading of the CAF compartment a FAP radioligand targets. ⚠ The nearest RADIOLIGAND datapoint is still one case of CONVENTIONAL chondrosarcoma (PMID 35025783), a different disease."
],

